YugabyteDB: add the TargetParser LLVM component to IWYU's link list.

iwyu_driver.cc calls llvm::sys::getDefaultTargetTriple(), which lives in the
LLVMTargetParser component in LLVM 21 (it was previously in Support). IWYU's
LLVM_LINK_COMPONENTS list omits TargetParser and relies on it being pulled in
transitively. That works when linking against static LLVM archives, but the
YugabyteDB thirdparty build links the toolchain's per-component shared dylibs
(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON), and shared linking does not pull transitive component
dependencies -- exactly the situation IWYU already documents for Serialization
a few lines below. Without this, the link fails with:

  ld64.lld: error: undefined symbol: llvm::sys::getDefaultTargetTriple()

Listing TargetParser explicitly puts libLLVMTargetParser on the link line.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@
 set(LLVM_LINK_COMPONENTS
   Option
   Support
+  TargetParser
   AllTargetsAsmParsers
   AllTargetsDescs
   AllTargetsInfos
